<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: center">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: right"><B>Filed pursuant to Rule 424(b)(3)</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: right"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>Registration
Statement No. 333-270674 </B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: center"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>SMX
(SECURITY MATTERS) PUBLIC LIMITED COMPANY </B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: center"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: center"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>Issuance
of up to 4,516,464 Ordinary Shares </B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: 24.5pt"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">This
prospectus relates to the resale, from time to time of up to 4,516,464 ordinary shares of the Company, $0.0001 par value per share, by
YA II PN, LTD, a Cayman Islands exempt limited partnership (&#8220;Yorkville&#8221;). The ordinary shares included in this prospectus
consist of ordinary shares that we may, in our discretion, elect to issue and sell to Yorkville, from time to time after the date of
this prospectus, pursuant to a Reciprocal Standby Equity Purchase Agreement we entered into with Yorkville on February 23, 2023 and became
effective on March 7, 2023 (the &#8220;SEPA&#8221;), in which Yorkville has committed to purchase from us up to $25,000,000 of our ordinary
shares, subject to the terms and conditions specified in the SEPA. As of the date of this prospectus, we have not issued any ordinary
shares to Yorkville pursuant to an Advance (as defined below), although we expect to have borrowed an aggregate of $3.5 million from
Yorkville under the SEPA evidenced by promissory notes. See the section entitled, &#8220;<I>Committed Equity Financing</I>&#8221; for
a description of the SEPA and the section entitled, &#8220;<I>Selling Shareholder</I>&#8221; for additional information regarding Yorkville.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: 24.5pt"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: 24.5pt"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Subject
to the terms and conditions of the SEPA, we have the right from time to time at our discretion until April 1, 2026 (or earlier in the
event Yorkville shall have made payment of $25 million in Advances), to direct Yorkville to purchase a specified amount of our ordinary
shares (each such sale, an &#8220;Advance&#8221;) by delivering written notice to Yorkville (each, an &#8220;Advance Notice&#8221;).
While there is no mandatory minimum amount for any Advance, it may not exceed the lesser of (i) an amount equal to 100% of the average
of the daily traded amount (as defined in the SEPA) during the five consecutive trading days immediately preceding an Advance Notice,
or (ii) 1 million ordinary shares. The Ordinary Shares will be purchased at a price equal to (i) 96% of the daily volume weighted average
price (&#8220;VWAP&#8221;) of our ordinary shares during the period commencing upon receipt by us of written confirmation of acceptance
of the Advance Notice by Yorkville, and ending on 4:00 p.m. New York City time on the applicable Advance Notice date, subject to a volume
threshold as described in the SEPA or (ii) 97% of the lowest daily VWAP of the ordinary shares during the three consecutive trading days
commencing on the Advance Notice Date; provided, however, that with respect to any clause (ii) Advance, we may establish a minimum acceptable
price in each Advance Notice below which we will not be obligated to make any sales to Yorkville.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: 24.5pt"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: 24.5pt"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: 24.5pt"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">We
will control the timing and amount of any sales of ordinary shares to Yorkville, except with respect to conversions of the Pre-Paid
Advances. Actual sales of our ordinary shares to Yorkville as an Advance under the SEPA will depend on a variety of factors
to be determined by us from time to time, which may include, among other things, market conditions, the trading price of our ordinary
shares and determinations by us as to the appropriate sources of funding for our business and operations. In addition, at any time during
the term of the SEPA, provided that there is a balance remaining outstanding under any of the promissory notes referred to above, Yorkville
may cause an Advance Notice to be deemed delivered to us and the issuance and sale of our ordinary shares to Yorkville pursuant to an
Advance, in accordance with the terms and subject to the limitations set forth in the SEPA.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: 24.5pt"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: 24.5pt"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Our
registration of the securities covered by this prospectus does not mean that Yorkville will offer or sell any of the ordinary shares.
Yorkville may offer, sell or distribute all or a portion of their ordinary shares publicly or through private transactions at prevailing
market prices or at negotiated prices. We will not receive any proceeds from the sale of ordinary shares by Yorkville pursuant to this
prospectus. However, we may receive up to $25,000,000 in aggregate gross proceeds from sales of our ordinary shares to Yorkville that
we may, in our discretion, elect to make, from time to time after the date of this prospectus, pursuant to the SEPA. We provide more
information about how Yorkville may sell or otherwise dispose of our ordinary shares in the section entitled, &#8220;<I>Plan of Distribution</I>.&#8221;
Yorkville is an &#8220;underwriter&#8221; within the meaning of Section 2(a)(11) of the Securities Act of 1933, as amended.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: 24.5pt"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: 24.5pt"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">We
are a &#8220;foreign private issuer&#8221; as defined under applicable Securities and Exchange Commission (&#8220;SEC&#8221;) rules and
an &#8220;emerging growth company&#8221; as that term is defined in the Jumpstart Our Business Startups Act of 2012 (the &#8220;JOBS
Act&#8221;) and are eligible for reduced public company disclosure requirements.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: 24.5pt"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: 24.5pt"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Our
ordinary shares are listed on The Nasdaq Global Market (&#8220;Nasdaq&#8221;) under the symbol &#8220;SMX&#8221; and our public warrants
are listed on The Nasdaq Capital Market under the symbol &#8220;SMXWW&#8221;. On May 19, 2023, the closing price of our ordinary
shares was $1.03.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"></FONT></P>

