    <TD STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 0.25in; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">(k)</FONT></TD>
    <TD STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Represents
    the effects of the recapitalization at Closing where Security Matters is the accounting acquirer, and the elimination of historical
    issued capital and additional paid in capital and accumulated losses of Lionheart. The adjustment as a reduction in retained earnings
    reflects the difference between the fair value of the shares deemed to have been issued to Lionheart shareholders by Security Matters
    and the fair value of Lionheart&#8217;s net assets acquired, in accordance with IFRS 2. The adjustment reflects the number of shares
    reflecting the actual Redemptions of 97.58%.</FONT></TD></TR>
